# Cloudflare Pages headers. The app is same-origin except ONE deliberate hole:
# `connect-src` also allows raw.githubusercontent.com, where the font picker
# fetches a picked family's commit-pinned face bytes + licence text (the app's
# own fetch layer re-checks every such URL against the same origin allowlist
# and size caps). `wasm-unsafe-eval` is the ONLY script relaxation (required to
# instantiate WebAssembly); there is no inline-script allowance. `style-src`
# permits inline styles (Vite injects the app stylesheet inline and React uses
# style attributes) — inline STYLE only, never inline script. Specimen fonts
# are constructed from fetched bytes via `new FontFace(…, buffer)`, which needs
# no `font-src` relaxation. Two `blob:` allowances, both for object URLs the
# app itself mints: `img-src` (the image codec decodes a pasted/placed/GIF/WebP
# image through `new Image()` on a Blob URL) and `frame-src` (the PDF download
# dialog previews the rendered PDF in an iframe on a Blob URL). `object-src`
# stays 'none' — the browser's PDF viewer in that frame does not need it.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://raw.githubusercontent.com; worker-src 'self'; frame-src blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
